      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SWAYZEE (11) called on his trademark courage to return to the winners' list here last week, racing parked before getting home by 1.6m. Has won five of eight tries at this longer distance so it should suit him better and he strikes at 50 per cent when third-up so should be further improved. He can overcome the outside barrier to deliver again. ROYAL CRUISER (9) was last seen when second in the Breeders Challenge 4EG Final a year ago and won twice in a row here prior so he is a talent. Draws wide but was readied with a solid trial and is a two-time fresh winner. RIPP (10) did a good job to come from this barrier and place behind SWAYZEE last week. He is a trifecta player again. ITS CONFIDENTIAL (2) draws much better than last week and is two from two at this longer distance so could be an improver.",
